  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of Resettlement Activities in West and Central Africa and the Great Lakes Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide transportation and other assistance to refugees from West and Central Africa and Great Lakes for resettlement to USA. These activities are part of the United States Refugee Admissions Program (USRAP) and fall under the Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between the US State Department/Bureau of Population, Refugees, and Migration (BPRM) and IOM. The support provided follows the program structure and reporting lines as established through the said MOU and the IOM General Instruction from 2011.</narrative>
  </description>
